-# libSceAgcDriver
-
-## add Functional
-
-- [EVENT_WRITE PIXEL_PIPE_STAT_CONTROL](../../../core/libs/prx/libSceAgcDriver/Execution/src/Pm4.cpp) (libSceAgcDriver, opcode 0x46, event 0x38) - not measured on a console. Only the 16-bit `instance_enable` mask is modelled ([PAL](https://github.com/GPUOpen-Drivers/pal/blob/c5e800072a32f68b6ccc4422936d96167c6e0728/src/core/hw/gfxip/gfx9/chip/gfx9_plus_merged_f32_me_pm4_packets.h#L1716-L1738) layout): dumps write and Z-pass predication sums only the enabled blocks. AnyPS5 counts samples for the whole target, so the lowest enabled block holds them all. The mask starts at all 16 blocks; only the `sceAgcAcbResetQueue` dispatch reset restores it, and `CLEAR_STATE` (`sceAgcDcbResetQueue`) keeps it, which the console may not. Counters other than occlusion count 0, strides other than 128 bits, reserved bits and a non-zero fourth dword throw. Whether the console's predication reads disabled blocks is not known, so Z-pass predication after a mask of 0 throws instead of guessing a result.
-
-## change [SET_PREDICATION]
-
-- [SET_PREDICATION](../../../core/libs/prx/libSceAgcDriver/Execution/src/Pm4.cpp) (AGC driver) - not measured on a console. Primitive-count predication, the CONTINUE bit, a predicated COND_EXEC, predicated command buffer chains and flips in predicated command buffers throw. Boolean predication follows the AMD PM4 encoding [Mesa](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/main/src/amd/common/sid.h) uses: operation 3 reads 64 bits, 4 reads 32 bits, and bit 8 runs predicated packets on a non-zero value (clear: on zero). Z-pass predication (operation 1) sums `end - begin` over the counter pairs a ZPASS_DONE dump writes (16-byte stride, bit 63 marks a written counter), as radeonsi lays out occlusion results, for the blocks the queue's last `PIXEL_PIPE_STAT_CONTROL` enabled (all 16 without one); an unwritten pair runs the packets under the bit 12 no-wait hint and throws under the wait hint. The address must have its low 4 bits clear, as `sceAgcDcbSetPredication` writes it
